# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  DISABLED — workflow renamed to `.disabled` to prevent GitHub Actions
# from loading it. To re-enable, rename back to `release-please.yml`.
#
# Why disabled (see BRANCHING.md + RELEASING.md for the full policy):
#   • OpenSquad cuts releases via short-lived `release/0.X.Y` branches
#     (PR → main → tag → absorb → delete). The release captain does the
#     version bump and CHANGELOG update by hand on that branch.
#   • release-please would open its own Release PR on every push to main,
#     racing with the human-driven flow and producing a second version of
#     `pyproject.toml` / `CHANGELOG.md` to reconcile. The auto-PR is
#     also routed against `main`, not `dev`, which conflicts with our
#     "dev is the integration line, main only ships releases" model.
#   • Kept here (and the config in `.github/disabled/release-please-config.json`)
#     as documentation of what release-please would do, in case we ever
#     want to flip to an automated-only flow. Both files live under
#     `.github/disabled/` so the dead state is obvious; to re-enable,
#     move them back to `.github/` and `.github/workflows/` respectively
#     and rename the workflow to `release-please.yml`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# release-please — opens a "Release PR" on every push to main.
#
# What it does:
#   1. Scans commits since the last release (Conventional Commits)
#   2. Bumps `pyproject.toml` to the next SemVer
#   3. Rewrites CHANGELOG.md grouped by type
#   4. Opens (or updates) a PR titled "chore(main): release X.Y.Z"
#      Once that PR is merged, release-please pushes a `vX.Y.Z` tag,
#      which in turn triggers the existing `.github/workflows/release.yml`
#      (Docker build + PyPI publish + GitHub Release).
#
# Branch model: this project ships from `main` only (releases branch
# off main, soak happens via `vX.Y.Z-beta.N` tags). For projects
# using a separate `dev` branch, add `"branches": [{ "branch": "dev" }]`
# and a second config under `.github/release-please-dev.json` if
# you want a different version cadence.
name: release-please

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

permissions:
  contents: write
  pull-requests: write
  id-token: write

jobs:
  release-please:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: googleapis/release-please-action@v4
        id: release
        with:
          config-file: .github/release-please-config.json
          # Default release-type is taken from config; explicit for clarity.
          release-type: python
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
      - name: Log release-please outcome
        if: steps.release.outputs.release_created == 'true'
        run: |
          echo "Release PR opened/updated for ${{ steps.release.outputs.tag_name }}"
          echo "Tag: ${{ steps.release.outputs.tag_name }}"
          echo "Major bump: ${{ steps.release.outputs.major }}"
          echo "Minor bump: ${{ steps.release.outputs.minor }}"
          echo "Patch bump: ${{ steps.release.outputs.patch }}"
